WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
Speaker 1: Let's talk about deceptive headlines&nbsp;
that can be written to achieve political goals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.320
I hope that this segment is a good snapshot&nbsp;
of how headlines can be used to distort and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:17.280
to influence and to push a particular narrative&nbsp;
that may be interesting to one media outlet versus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.760
another. So what happened? While Joe Biden was&nbsp;
recently asked during his current trip to Asia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.720
about Chinese aggression towards Taiwan, now&nbsp;
that's a legitimate issue. We've talked about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:33.280
it on this program. Will China see the chaos of&nbsp;
what's happening in Ukraine thanks to the Russian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:40.480
invasion, as maybe an opening in which they could&nbsp;
make a military move against Taiwan? So China,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.960
Taiwan, that's the issue. It's a real issue.&nbsp;
It's a legitimate issue. President Joe Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:52.880
was asked about it and Joe Biden confirmed if&nbsp;
China invaded Taiwan, the U.S. would intervene.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:58.400
And that's been American policy for a long time.&nbsp;
So let's look at the actual question and answer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.920
This is the source material for the topic and&nbsp;
the subsequent headlines we're going to look at.&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:09.200
Speaker 2: It didn't want to get involved in the&nbsp;
Ukraine conflict militarily for obvious reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.520
Are you willing to get involved militarily&nbsp;
to defend Taiwan if it comes to that?&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.360
Speaker 3: Yes.
Speaker 2: You are.&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:21.520
Speaker 3: That's a commitment we made.
Speaker 1: Okay. So that's not news. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.640
there's nothing there that's actually newsworthy.&nbsp;
There's something called the one-China policy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.760
You can agree with the one-China policy or you&nbsp;
can disagree with it. But the policy has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:39.360
dating all the way back to 1979. It was first&nbsp;
started stated in 1972. The U.S. acknowledges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.280
that China on either side of the Taiwan Strait,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:50.880
maintain there is but one China and that Taiwan&nbsp;
is a part of China. That's the United States&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:58.560
position. Now, in 2016, Donald Trump said the U.S.&nbsp;
isn't necessarily bound by the one-China policy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.040
And lots of people said, oh my goodness, Trump&nbsp;
is trying to change the one-China policy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:09.120
But then in a phone call in 2017 that Trump had&nbsp;
with Xi Jinping, they talked about a number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:15.040
different things. And Trump agreed at the request&nbsp;
of President Xi to honor the one-China policy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:20.400
Okay, so we have that. We also have&nbsp;
the Taiwan Relations Act from 1979,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.880
and we have the six assurances, as they're&nbsp;
called, that Reagan gave to Taiwan in 1982,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:37.680
which say that if Taiwan violates the principles&nbsp;
the U.S. believes in, or if a rather if China&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:44.080
violates the principles that the U.S. believes&nbsp;
in, the U.S. would help Taiwan to defend itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:50.160
if if China were to invade, the United States&nbsp;
would help Taiwan in that situation. So this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:55.120
has been policy for a really long time. So Biden&nbsp;
is asked during the press conference, well, if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.480
China attacks, would the U.S. help defend Taiwan&nbsp;
in the United States? President says, yes, that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:06.240
the commitment we made. It's not news. Biden&nbsp;
is essentially saying the stuff we've agreed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:13.920
for the last 40 years, we're going to abide by it.&nbsp;
That's it. That's the story. Check out how every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:20.720
News Corp media outlet covered it. And by&nbsp;
meet by News Corp, we mean Fox, Fox Business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:26.960
Wall Street Journal. The Wall Street Journal&nbsp;
titled their article Bill Biden Says U.S. Would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:36.240
Intervene Militarily If China Invaded Taiwan. Fox&nbsp;
News says U.S. military will defend Taiwan if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:44.480
comes to that, Biden says. Fox Business Segment&nbsp;
Says Biden Says U.S. will intervene if China&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:51.600
invades Taiwan. Now, again, it's not about these&nbsp;
headlines being literally false. It's the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:57.920
that they're being written specifically to further&nbsp;
the idea of Biden's out there looking for wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:03.600
Biden's out there looking for military conflict,&nbsp;
and it was Trump who was keeping us out of wars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:09.600
This has been the narrative in the George W Bush&nbsp;
era, the right loved war. They loved spreading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:14.160
democracy and all of this different stuff. And&nbsp;
then Trump came in and Trump said the Iraq war was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:18.880
a bad idea, even though previously Trump had said,&nbsp;
I would have gone into Iraq. Doesn't matter. Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:24.480
came in and said Iraq was bad, which is true. Just&nbsp;
he's a hypocrite on it. And he said, Hillary will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:27.840
get us into wars, but I won't. I'm going to keep&nbsp;
us out of wars and get us out of more places.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.080
And then the claim made about Joe Biden was&nbsp;
Biden's going to get us into wars, Biden's blood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:39.840
thirsty, Biden's war hungry, even though there&nbsp;
was no such evidence of that. And so they want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:45.280
to write headlines that will further that. And&nbsp;
most of the Fox audience probably doesn't realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:51.200
most of the Wall Street Journal audience doesn't&nbsp;
realize the U.S. has previously said we would help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:57.680
to defend Taiwan in such a case. Biden's not&nbsp;
treading new ground here. Biden's not changing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:03.760
policy. He's not an. Announcing new policy.&nbsp;
But the story that Fox wants to tell is here's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:08.560
Biden once again looking for military problem. So&nbsp;
they'll say, look at Biden wanting to intervene.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:15.040
Look at Biden wanting to interject and inject&nbsp;
the military. The truth is, Biden saying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:20.480
I'm not changing the 40 year policy that we've&nbsp;
had now comparatively. Reuters had a more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:27.200
straightforward headline for this story. Reuters&nbsp;
called it No Change in U.S. Policy towards Taiwan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:34.080
says White House Official. Now, it's not only Fox&nbsp;
opting for the more salacious headlines, most of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:40.880
them do it. CNN had a similar one, but it's at&nbsp;
least more fair. CNN's headline was Biden says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:48.320
U.S. Would Respond Militarily If China Attacked&nbsp;
Taiwan, but White House insists there is no policy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:53.840
change and indeed there isn't. So it's really&nbsp;
important to understand how to research these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.840 --> 00:06:03.280
things directly. If you were to Google one China&nbsp;
policy six assurances to Taiwan, U.S. relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.560
to China and Taiwan, you would realize there's&nbsp;
not a newsworthy element here. Joe Biden is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:14.880
saying like, yeah, this is the policy and we're&nbsp;
going to stick to the policy. The story is Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:21.680
doesn't unilaterally change anything when it comes&nbsp;
to China and Taiwan. That doesn't really make for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:29.440
a very exciting headline. So that's the genesis,&nbsp;
the oranges, for lack of a better term, of a bunch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:34.160
of these headlines and hopefully instructive in&nbsp;
understanding how these narratives can be woven.

